-- title:
--   Labelled level automorphisms suffice to reach Igusa discs, q=3
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ with $q=3$, a non-zero $M'$ not divisible by $q$, and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell\equiv 11\pmod{12}$ and $\ell\mid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $q$ a non-unit of $A$, let $W$ be a finite set of places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}$ of level $M'$ over the residue field of $A$, let $R_0$ be a constant reduction of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$ (contained in $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ via `hle`) to that field, and let $\zeta$ be a primitive $q$th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let `OIg` assign a valuation subring of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ to each point of $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$, the one at `lineInfty` being the Gauss ring: $f$ belongs to it exactly when $f\cdot y=x$ for Laurent series $x,y$ over $A$ with $y$ having non-zero coefficientwise reduction. Let $R$ be a regular prolongation of $A$ on $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ with residue field $\mathrm{xHFunctionFieldC}$ of level $q^2M'$ and subgroup $\mathrm{levelH}\ q\ M'$, whose ring of integers is that Gauss ring; let `NIg` be a finite set of places of the residue function field and `disc` assign to each such place a set of places of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$. Assume that every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\ q\ M'\ \zeta'\ \gamma$ ($\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$, $\zeta'$ arbitrary) which preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$ induces a residue automorphism $R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau$ whose action on places preserves `NIg` (`hNstab`) and satisfies $\mathrm{smulDisc}\,\tau(\mathrm{disc}\,Q)=\mathrm{disc}(R.\mathrm{resAut}\,\tau\cdot Q)$ for $Q\notin$ `NIg` (`hdiscstab`). Call a place $P$ of $\mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ untubed if for no $s\in W$ is it true that for every $f$ in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ regular at all places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$ where $j$ is regular, whenever $R_0.\mathrm{residue}\,f$ lies in the valuation ring of $s$ and $a\in A$ has residue $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue}\,f)$, the difference $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)-a$ lies in $A$ and in its maximal ideal. Assume (`hδ`) every untubed $P$ is carried by some $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\ q\ M'\ \zeta\ \gamma$ with $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ into $\mathrm{disc}\,Q$ for some $Q\notin$ `NIg`, and let $g$ assign to each point $x\in\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$ an automorphism lying in that subgroup and of the form $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\ q\ M'\ \zeta\ \gamma$ for some $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ with $\mathrm{redQ}\ q\ \gamma\cdot\mathrm{lineInfty}\ q=x$. Then for every untubed place $P$ there are a point $x$ and a place $Q\notin$ `NIg` with $g(x)\cdot P\in\mathrm{disc}\,Q$.
--
--   This is the step in the assembly of the semistable covering of $X_{\Gamma_H(q^2M')}$ which replaces the unspecified level automorphism furnished by the tube analysis with one from the fixed finite labelling $g$ indexed by $\mathbb{P}^1(\mathbb{Z}/q)$, the cusps of the Igusa components; it is the case $q=3$, where the extra hypotheses on $\ell$ serve as a rigidity guard. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted_of_eq_three_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_semistableCovering_equivClauses_of_valuationSubrings_semistableModel_inertiaInfty_charted_of_eq_three_of_dvd).
